course: dictionary
lesson: 11917
title: Short words with big meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some short words are shortcuts. «ca.» is short for the Latin word «circa», and it means about or around. You will often see it in history books and on museum labels: «The vase was made ca. 1500.» That means it was made about the year 1500, not exactly in that year.
explain: A full stop after a short word often shows it has been cut short. «ca.» and «c.» both mean about. Ca without a full stop, with a capital C, can mean something else entirely: in science it is the chemical symbol for calcium.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to use. A date after it means about. A science lesson about bones or chalk means calcium. An address with CA means California. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
fact: ca. or c. is short for the Latin word «circa», which means about or around.
fact: «The castle was built ca. 1200.» means the castle was built about the year 1200.
fact: Ca, in science, is the chemical symbol for calcium, a mineral found in bones, milk and chalk.
fact: CA is short for California on US addresses, and «.ca» at the end of a website address means Canada.
fact: «Ça va?» is French and means «How are you?». It is not an English word.
exercise: «The bridge was built ca. 1800.» What does ca. mean here? | Exactly, on that very day | *About or around | Not at all | Very quickly
exercise: In a science lesson, Ca is the chemical symbol for which element? | Copper | Carbon | *Calcium | Iron
exercise: What does the French «Ça va?» mean? | Goodbye, see you soon | *How are you? | Thank you very much | Where is the station?
test: On a US address, CA usually stands for which place? | *California | Cardiff | Cairo | Canada
test: A website address ending in .ca belongs to which country? | Chile | Cyprus | *Canada | Cuba
exam: «The mountain was formed ca. 300 million years ago.» Which meaning fits best? | *About 300 million years ago | Exactly 300 million years ago | In the year 300 AD | Very recently
